#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0252-B expect=violation domain=ADDL
#note "NEW with the M2-P5 ruling (option (a), Fix #305) - the pin that the ADDL widening landed. PMDA ADaM row 200's DOMAINS cell lists eight tokens; before this ruling seven were reachable across the five-way AD0252 split and ADDL was reachable from none, because DEVICE LEVEL ANALYSIS DATASET has NO supertype in AdamDataStructureDetector.SUPERTYPES (owner decision 2026-08-09, deliberate and correct). Adding the token to -B's Scope.Data_Structures.Include is the corpus's own idiom for the ADSL/ADDL pair (PMDA-AD0355, PMDA-AD0570). structure=\"DEVICE LEVEL ANALYSIS DATASET\" is the full token - only ADSL/BDS/OCCDS/OTHER have shortcuts. Two prohibited record-level names on a per-device dataset -> Variable Metadata Check, one finding per offending column, pinned by variable_name with no row=."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
#expectViolationCount 2
#expectViolationAt variable_name=PARAMCD
#expectViolationAt variable_name=AVAL
dataset ADDL structure="DEVICE LEVEL ANALYSIS DATASET"
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col SPDEVID type=Char
col PARAMCD type=Char
col AVAL    type=Num
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | DEV01 | ALB | 30
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1023 | DEV02 | ALB | 31
